# Re-include the research records under this tree.
#
# These records are .txt (per-day chain and EXPLAIN output), .log (run logs) and
# .csv (measure tables) by nature. The repository root .gitignore excludes those
# globally -- lines 33 (*.log), 43 (*.csv) and 44 (*.txt) -- which silently drops
# 1,255 of the 3,528 files intended for this commit: `git add` succeeds, `git
# status` reports nothing untracked, and the records are simply absent.
#
# Fixed with a negation rule rather than `git add -f`, per
# .claude/rules/data-access.md: the force flag works once and hides the same
# problem from the next file added here.
#
# Scope is this directory and below only. The root patterns still apply
# everywhere else in the repository.

!*.txt
!*.log
!*.csv
